          "explanation": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&times;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&times;</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>0.5</mn></mfrac><mo>&times;</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n<p>= 1000</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "69452fa69537319e1ec34b5d",
          "question": "<p>A simple microscope has a focal length of \\( 5 \\mathrm{~cm} \\). The magnification at the least distance of distinct vision is-</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>1</p>",
            "<p>5</p>",
            "<p>4</p>",
            "<p>6</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3,
          "explanation": "<p>The given focal length of the simple microscope is \\(f=5\\text{\\ cm}\\). The standard value for the least distance of distinct vision is \\(D=25\\text{ cm}\\). These values are substituted into the magnification formula: \\(M=1+\\frac{25\\text{\\ cm}}{5\\text{cm}}\\). The division is performed: \\(\\frac{25}{5}=5\\). The result is added to \\(1\\): \\(M=1+5=6\\).</p>"
